From 660bd3170568a8dc19da9219d8b11f424a5c6116 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amelie Delaunay <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 15:05:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 416/913] dt-bindings: dma: align st,stm32-dma3.yaml with v6.18
 kernel for OSTL V7

Several updates after upstream and STM32MP21 support:
- one dma-cell has been dropped (now 3 instead of 4),
- the compatible st,stm32-dma3 has been updated to st,stm32mp25-dma3,
  and st,stm32mp21-dma3 has been added,
- st,axi-max-burst-len has been dropped, the AXI maximum burst length is
  now managed through the compatible,
- st,syscfg-arcr has been added to support AXI address remapping
  configuration on STM32MP21,
- examples have been updated accordingly,
- fix st,protreg alignment by removing extra useless `properties:`.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 718e170f836c43b95c24e402f25b24a98a408bf1 dt-bindings: dma: align st,stm32-dma3.yaml with v6.18 kernel for OSTL V7]
Signed-off-by: Amelie Delaunay <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I9de74d26ab11ed33b5bf52c46c94df06b77b5a3b
